  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is TMR? What is the main goal of TMR feeding? List the five key components/ingredients required to formulate a balanced ration in TMR. (6 marks)', 'TMR (total mixed ration) is a feeding method in which all ingredients - forages, concentrates, minerals and vitamins - are weighed and thoroughly mixed so each mouthful is nutritionally balanced. Goal: provide a balanced diet in every bite, stabilise rumen fermentation, prevent selective eating and raise intake, milk yield and health. Components: (1) roughage/forage (silage, hay, green fodder); (2) energy concentrates (maize, grains, bran); (3) protein sources (oil cakes, soybean meal); (4) minerals and vitamins (mineral mixture, salt); (5) water and additives (buffers, molasses) for the right moisture.', null, '[{"point": "TMR: total mixed ration - all feeds mixed into one uniform ration", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Goal: every bite balanced; stable rumen, higher intake and production", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Five components: forage/roughage, energy concentrate, protein, minerals and vitamins, water/additives", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
