  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'Discuss the multifactorial nature of mastitis in dairy cows. Explain the key roles of environmental and infectious factors in its occurrence. Propose a comprehensive mastitis control program for a commercial dairy farm, detailing the management practices for both milking and dry periods. (20 marks)', 'Mastitis arises from the interaction of the cow (stage of lactation, high yield, teat injury, immunity, nutrition), pathogens and the environment.
Infectious factors: contagious organisms (Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus agalactiae, Mycoplasma) spread cow to cow at milking by hands, cloths and liners; environmental organisms (E. coli, Klebsiella, Streptococcus uberis) come from dung, wet bedding and dirty yards.
Environmental factors: poor hygiene, wet or dirty housing, faulty milking machines (vacuum, liners), poor milking technique, overcrowding, heat stress and fly load.
Control programme - milking: clean, dry udders; fore-strip and check milk; pre-dip and post-dip teats; individual towels; gloves; milk infected cows last; maintain the machine; monitor SCC and use CMT; treat clinical cases promptly and record.
Dry period: blanket or selective dry-cow antibiotic therapy and internal teat sealant; clean, dry calving and dry-cow areas; balanced nutrition (vitamin E, selenium); cull chronically infected cows; keep records and work with a veterinarian.', null, '[{"point": "Multifactorial: host, pathogen and environment interacting", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Infectious (contagious: Staph. aureus, Strep. agalactiae; environmental: E. coli, Strep. uberis) and environmental factors (bedding, hygiene, milking machine)", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Milking-time control: hygiene, pre/post-dipping, stripping, milking order, machine maintenance, CMT", "marks": 6}, {"point": "Dry period: dry cow therapy/teat sealant, clean dry housing, culling chronic cases, records, nutrition", "marks": 4}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'animal-science'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 20,
