  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'Discuss the principles of biosecurity in modern livestock farming. Explain how a well-designed biosecurity program can mitigate the risk of disease outbreaks, improve herd health, and enhance overall farm productivity. Provide specific examples of internal and external biosecurity measures. (20 marks)', 'Biosecurity is the set of measures that keep disease out of a farm (external) and stop it spreading within the farm (internal). Its principles are segregation (keep animals away from sources of infection), cleaning (remove dirt that shelters pathogens) and disinfection, supported by monitoring and records.
Benefits: fewer outbreaks of diseases such as FMD, avian influenza or ASF; lower mortality and treatment costs; less antibiotic use; better growth, fertility and yield; access to markets; protection of public health from zoonoses.
External measures: buy animals from known healthy sources and quarantine them (2-4 weeks); fence the farm; control visitors and vehicles; footbaths and farm clothing; rodent, bird and wildlife control; safe feed and water.
Internal measures: all-in/all-out systems; separate age groups; isolation pens for sick animals; clean and disinfect pens and equipment; vaccination and deworming schedules; proper disposal of carcasses and manure; staff training and records.', null, '[{"point": "Principles: segregation, cleaning, disinfection (also traceability)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Mitigates outbreaks, better herd health, lower costs and higher productivity", "marks": 5}, {"point": "External measures (quarantine, controlled visitors/vehicles, sourcing, fencing, footbaths)", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Internal measures (all-in-all-out, sick pens, hygiene, vaccination, carcass disposal, records)", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation') and t.slug = 'animal-science'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-3'), 'standard', 20,
