  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'Analyze the key factors to consider when developing a farm business plan for a new livestock enterprise. Discuss the importance of market analysis, financial projections, and risk management in ensuring the long-term sustainability and profitability of the operation. (20 marks)', 'Key factors: clear goals; choice of enterprise and breed suited to climate and market; site, land and water; feed and fodder supply; housing and equipment; labour and skills; veterinary services; regulations and permits (e.g. from the Department of Livestock).
Market analysis: who will buy, how much and at what price; competitors and imports; seasonal demand; marketing channels (cooperatives, schools, hotels). It prevents producing what cannot be sold.
Financial projections: start-up capital, operating costs, expected income, cash-flow forecast, break-even point and loan repayment. They show whether the enterprise is viable and are needed to get finance.
Risk management: disease (biosecurity, vaccination), price falls, feed shortages, climate events, theft; tools include insurance, diversification, contracts, reserves and contingency plans.
Together these keep the farm profitable and sustainable over the long term.', null, '[{"point": "Key factors: goals, choice of species/breed, location, feed, labour, infrastructure, regulations", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Market analysis: demand, competitors, prices, channels", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Financial projections: capital, operating costs, cash flow, break-even, financing", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Risk management: disease, prices, climate, insurance, diversification, contingency", "marks": 5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'subject-specialisation'),
